A||||12||sluppy123||Grand Am Brakes III||||8||
Z||000000||sluppy123||03-21-2000||10:30 PM||||Just finished installing my new Grand Am vented rotors and new Blazer master cylinder. Everything bolted right up and I thought everything was going to work, but all is not well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I finished bleeding all the claipers and the MS, jump in the car to test the pedel feel........... <B>Softer than SH**</B> So i bleed everything again, Still soft, Bleed them again still soft. I give up.<P>Anybody have any advice or suggestions???<P>TIA-Brian||||reg||8
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||03-21-2000||10:55 PM||||Master cylinder from a full size Blazer?<BR>Soft as in, easy to actuate, or soft as in spungy? What method did you use to bleed the brakes? Furthest to closest or vice versa? Presure bleed or vacuum? Give more details! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sluppy123||03-21-2000||11:14 PM||||Master cylinder is from a 94' full size 4X4 Blazer. The calipers were Bleed starting with the Furthest(RR) from the MS and working my way to the closest (LF). I tried both Vacuum bleeding them and Pressure bleeding them. <P>The best way I can decribe the pedle is that it starts out being soft & spungy then it feels like it's going to stop, but it still goes all the way to the floor. so it does build up pressure, enough to stop the car, but not enough to turn off the warning light or to lock the wheels.<P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-22-2000||12:22 AM||||It's best to bench bleed master cylinders first before installing them. Sounds like maybe you still have air in the system. Can I ask a stupid question? Why did you use the full size Blazer M/C? Maybe you have a good reason, but in my opinion, that's way too big for your setup. Ever compare full size truck calipers to Grand Am calipers? When I do my M/C swap, it'll be with a S-10 unit.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||03-22-2000||08:47 AM||||Your first note said nothing specific about the rear brakes. Are they still stock? The symptoms you discribed in your second note sound like the rear brakes may need further machanical adjustment. If this isn't it you may need to install an adjustable proportioning valve.<P>Roy L.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||03-22-2000||11:43 AM||||Here are a few links to articles on the swap with the part nubmbers and the reason for the full size master. <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/realbrakes/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/realbrakes/index.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/86se.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/86se.html</A>  <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-grandambrakes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-grandambrakes.html</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||sluppy123||03-22-2000||04:18 PM||||Batboy- This is the site that says to use a Full size Blazer MS, and not to use a S-10 MS.    <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/86se.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/86se.html</A> <P>Also, The master cylinder was bench bled before instalation.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 03-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||03-22-2000||09:08 PM||||Ok, maybe I'm wrong. Seems like overkill though.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GREENDANO||03-22-2000||09:37 PM||||I used the 4WD 4 wheel disc brake MC and had to use two feet to stop my GT.  I put a new, stock Fiero MC on instead and lost a pedal reserve but gained  "Holy Cow!!!!" stopping ability when I did my GA swap.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000010||FIEROCIOUS||03-22-2000||10:48 PM||||Batboy, The S-10 won't work as it is backwards F/R. <P>The Blazer master cylinder is smaller! Internaly! Just because the outward appearance is differant doesn't make it any worse or better. (words to live by)<BR>People over confuse hydralic systems, Think of it more as a lever to give leverage if you make the master cylinder smaller it takes the mechanical advatage away (makes pedal firmer) but requires less movement. If they were the same size (piston/master) It would be equaldistant/equaleffective.<P>I'm suspecting he's done the rear, If he hasn't done the rear yet he would lock his front easier! <P>So have you gravity bled them yet? What color is the brake fluid? Did you use ATF? J/K.<P>If the brake fluid is not clear keep bleeding!<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000011||DJRice||03-23-2000||11:39 AM||||Keep Bleeding...<P>Thats what I do whenever Im working on my Fiero. (at least from the knuckles)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||sluppy123||03-23-2000||06:11 PM||||The problem was found and fixed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>So you're wondering what the problem was???? <P>I got to thinking that maybe there was something wrong with the MS. So off it came and off I went to the parts store for a <B>NEW</B> MS, not a rebuilt one, on it went,  let the bleeding begin. vacuum bled everything in site. Crossed my fingers, said a prayer then stepped on the pedel, and to my amazement it didn't go to the floor. Praise the lord I got's Brakes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000013||kevin||03-24-2000||02:13 AM||||Good brakes are a blessing when passing a Jr. College and falling your eyes upon a beautiful blond volumptuos co-ed. Oh my, I guess the spring time season is upon me.||||reg||1
